from bank import add
add('F01',[('Buyer','The person or role authorized to approve the commercial engagement.'),('End user','The person who performs or benefits from the workflow in daily use.'),('Problem hypothesis','An unverified claim about recurring pain that discovery must investigate.')],('A demo enthusiast cannot approve budget or data access. What is the next discovery step?','Identify and involve the missing authorized decision makers.','Treat enthusiasm as a signed engagement.','Request the full private archive anyway.','User interest, spending authority and data authorization are distinct responsibilities.'),'Describe your offer without naming an AI tool. Who has the pain, who approves it, and what remains a hypothesis?')
add('F02',[('Observation','Something directly seen or heard in the actual discovery exercise.'),('Interpretation','Your explanation of what an observation might mean.'),('Disconfirming evidence','An observation that would weaken the proposed problem or solution hypothesis.')],('A client says a task occurs daily, but examples show twice a month. How should you record this?','Preserve the discrepancy and clarify actual volume.','Use daily volume because it improves the business case.','Discard the examples.','Discovery should investigate contradictions rather than choose the most favorable assumption.'),'Write three non-leading questions about a recent workflow instance and one answer that would make you decline the project.')
add('F03',[('Net time benefit','Baseline effort minus assisted processing, review, exception and other required work.'),('Scenario range','Conservative, expected and optimistic outcomes based on explicit assumptions.'),('Pilot success measure','An observable result agreed to test a material uncertainty.')],('Generation saves eight minutes but review adds six minutes per item. What belongs in the benefit model?','Both changes and any remaining exception or maintenance effort.','Only the eight-minute saving.','An assumption that all saved minutes become revenue.','A workflow benefit must include work that remains or increases, not just a faster generation step.'),'Create a conservative scenario that makes your project unattractive. Which assumption most changes the decision?')
add('F04',[('Service package','A bounded outcome with supported inputs, deliverables, exclusions and review duties.'),('Exclusion','A capability or effect that is explicitly outside the engagement.'),('Expansion gate','Evidence and a separate decision required before broadening scope.')],('Your pilot supports approved text notes. The buyer assumes scans and automatic emailing are included. What needs correction?','Make input boundaries and excluded external actions explicit in the offer.','Promise them because all documents are similar.','Leave the ambiguity until final delivery.','Hidden assumptions create scope and operational risk; a package must state what is actually included.'),'Write five exclusions for your service and explain how each protects a clear deliverable rather than avoiding legitimate work.')
add('F05',[('Statement of work','A planning document defining deliverables, responsibilities, dependencies and acceptance.'),('Acceptance condition','An agreed observable behavior on a named dataset and environment.'),('Change request','A documented proposal to alter scope with its cost, schedule and test impacts.')],('A client adds a new document format during final review. How should you handle it?','Assess it as a scope change against the agreed acceptance conditions.','Silently weaken existing acceptance checks.','Declare all formats supported without testing.','Acceptance refers to agreed conditions; new formats require an explicit impact and scope decision.'),'Write one happy-path and one failure acceptance scenario with named input, reviewer and observable output.')
add('F06',[('One-time effort','Work such as discovery, implementation, testing and initial handover.'),('Recurring cost','Ongoing usage, hosting, review or support effort after the initial build.'),('Contingency','Explicit planning allowance for uncertainty rather than hidden guaranteed profit.')],('Your estimate counts coding but omits testing, review and handover. What is the consequence?','It understates the effort needed to deliver the agreed outcome.','It becomes more accurate by focusing only on technical work.','Omitted work will automatically be free of effort.','A commercial delivery requires non-coding work; an honest estimate accounts for it separately.'),'Model doubled volume and increased exception review. Which recurring cost or capacity limit changes first?')
add('F07',[('Data-flow map','A record of inputs, destinations, processing, storage, logs and exports.'),('Data minimization','Using only the fields needed for the agreed task.'),('Access revocation','Removing implementer privileges while preserving client-owned operation.')],('A sample workbook includes a hidden sheet of learner names unrelated to the task. What should intake do?','Identify and remove unnecessary personal fields before any approved processing.','Upload the whole workbook because one sample was shared.','Copy names into the portfolio for realism.','Permission to inspect a sample is not blanket permission to distribute unrelated data.'),'List each data destination and account owner in your pilot. Which could still hold data after an apparent deletion?')
add('F08',[('Thin pilot','A narrow but complete end-to-end workflow that tests an agreed uncertainty.'),('Fake integration','A clearly labeled deterministic substitute for an external dependency.'),('Go/no-go evidence','Observed results that support continuing, conditioning or stopping an engagement.')],('A source note lacks an important concept. What should a draft-and-review pilot do?','Flag the missing source information and keep review visible.','Invent the concept to avoid an incomplete demo.','Hide the manual reviewer to appear automated.','A useful pilot exposes uncertainty and manual work instead of concealing them behind a polished output.'),'Describe one normal, one missing-information and one unavailable-dependency path that your pilot must demonstrate.')
add('F09',[('Defect','A behavior that violates an agreed acceptance condition.'),('Preference','A requested presentation change judged against the audience and rubric.'),('New requirement','Additional behavior or constraints outside the agreed scope.')],('Feedback requests translation into three languages absent from the agreement. How should it be classified?','A new requirement with scope and testing impacts.','Automatically a defect in the existing release.','A cosmetic wording change with no evaluation cost.','New language support changes capability and quality requirements; it needs an explicit decision.'),'Classify three feedback items from your pilot and show the different follow-up evidence each classification requires.')
add('F10',[('Client-readable evaluation','Results explained in terms of the agreed business task and limitations.'),('Fresh review set','Representative examples not used to tune the current candidate.'),('Conditional acceptance','Proceeding only with explicit unresolved conditions, owners and limits.')],('A 20-case pilot has 16 complete drafts, three clarification needs and one unsupported claim. What should the report include?','All categories, sample size and review effort.','A rounded success percentage with the failed case omitted.','A guarantee for arbitrary future volume.','A useful report preserves outcomes and scope rather than compressing unlike failures into a flattering headline.'),'Which observed failure blocks your acceptance condition, and which can remain a documented limitation? Explain the distinction.')
add('F11',[('Milestone','A reviewable artifact with acceptance, an owner and prerequisites.'),('Dependency','Something another activity needs before its claim can be completed.'),('Risk trigger','An observable condition that prompts a planned mitigation or escalation.')],('Client data access is delayed, so you test only synthetic fixtures. What may you claim?','Synthetic feasibility is observed; real-data validation remains pending.','Real-data acceptance is complete because code exists.','The dependency no longer matters.','Work can proceed on fixtures, but missing evidence must remain distinct from completed validation.'),'Define a dependency delay, the work that can continue, and the acceptance claim that must stay pending.')
add('F12',[('Scope impact','How a request changes behavior, data flows, tests, duties or schedule.'),('Operational effect','A change in external state such as sending messages or publishing content.'),('Alternative option','A smaller route to the buyer’s objective with explicitly different trade-offs.')],('A client asks to email handouts automatically. What belongs in the change assessment?','Recipient verification, permission, duplicate prevention, audit and recovery behavior.','Only the time to add an email field.','A promise that sending is risk-free.','External effects introduce operational requirements beyond interface data entry.'),'Offer a smaller alternative to one high-impact request and explain what objective it preserves and what it leaves manual.')
add('F13',[('Operational ownership','The party responsible for service accounts, data, recurring charges and incident response.'),('Recovery evidence','An observed restart or restore result rather than an unchecked backup file.'),('Credential separation','Client operation does not depend on an implementer’s private personal key.')],('Removing your personal account stops the client app. What handover issue does this reveal?','Operational ownership and credentials are still improperly dependent on you.','Successful access revocation.','Proof that support will never be needed.','A client-owned service needs an agreed account and permission structure that survives implementer departure.'),'Design an isolated restore check and an access-revocation rehearsal with concrete success observations.')
add('F14',[('Acceptance session','An authorized reviewer checks agreed scenarios and records their actual outcomes.'),('Not tested','No observation establishes whether a condition passes or fails.'),('Handover rehearsal','Another person uses the guide and system without continual author intervention.')],('A reviewer attended a polished demo but did not run the agreed scenarios. Is acceptance established?','No; the agreed acceptance checks still need observed outcomes.','Yes; attendance proves every requirement passed.','Yes; a screenshot substitutes for missing tests.','A demonstration and formal acceptance evidence are different activities.'),'Create a training case that reveals whether a user confuses a completed draft with an approved output.')
add('F15',[('Support scope','Defined coverage, environment, responsibilities and escalation assumptions.'),('Response target','A planned time to acknowledge or begin handling a report, distinct from guaranteed resolution.'),('Incident review','A record of observations, recovery and contributing conditions with testable corrective actions.')],('A provider changes its response format. What is an appropriate workflow response?','Fail safely, retain drafts, correct the adapter and rerun relevant evaluations.','Treat unreadable output as success.','Promise instant resolution of any upstream change.','Dependency changes need explicit failure behavior and regression evidence; support cannot guarantee unseen repairs.'),'Write an incident timeline involving stale policy content and identify two prevention checks tied to its cause.')
add('F16',[('Permissioned case study','A portfolio uses client identity or data only with appropriate permission.'),('Simulated engagement','A self-directed scenario accurately labeled rather than represented as a paying client.'),('Claim-evidence map','Each result statement points to its baseline, evaluation or implementation artifact.')],('A self-directed fictional project is described as a paying client success. What must change?','Label the simulation and show the actual implementation evidence.','Invent a testimonial to make it credible.','Keep the claim because the prototype works.','Implementation value does not justify fabricating customer identity or commercial results.'),'Audit three case-study claims. State sample size, scope and the artifact that supports each.')
add('F17',[('Qualification','Checking problem fit, authority, data feasibility, timing and review capacity.'),('Published fact','Information actually available from an identifiable public business source.'),('Outreach assumption','An unverified inference that should be phrased as a question, not an asserted problem.')],('A prospect’s website mentions live cohorts. Can you state that their handout process is inefficient?','No; treat that possible workflow problem as a discovery question.','Yes; cohorts prove operational pain.','Yes; every training company has identical bottlenecks.','A published business activity does not establish the specific inefficiency you want to sell against.'),'Draft a short introduction for a fictional prospect that separates an observed fact from a question about the workflow. Do not send it.')
add('F18',[('Delivery consistency','Offer, scope, implementation, acceptance and handover describe the same actual release.'),('Retrospective','A review of what happened and concrete improvements for the next engagement.'),('Reusable template','An adaptable structure based on tested delivery work rather than copied unexamined claims.')],('The final package promises scans, but evaluation covers text only. What should you do?','Implement and test scan support or narrow the claim before acceptance.','Leave the mismatch because the UI is polished.','Delete the evaluation scope statement.','Cross-document consistency requires capability evidence or a corrected promise.'),'Trace one promise from your offer through a tested implementation, acceptance record and handover instruction. Where is the weakest evidence?')
